| autocfg | 1.5.1 | Apache-2.0 OR MIT | num-traits' build script |
| cfg_aliases | 0.2.2 | MIT | the wgpu crates' and winit's build scripts |
| gl_generator | 0.14.0 | Apache-2.0 | glutin_wgl_sys' build script |
| khronos_api | 3.1.0 | Apache-2.0 | gl_generator |
| xml-rs | 0.8.29 | MIT | gl_generator |

**Proc-macro crates and what they need.** A proc macro is compiled for the build machine and
executed by the compiler while it expands attributes and derives. It emits code that ends up in
the binary; the macro crate itself does not. Neither do the ordinary libraries that exist in this
graph only to serve one, which is why `syn`, `quote`, and `proc-macro2` are absent from the count
even though they are not macros themselves:

