Neither group is distributed, so neither carries a notice obligation; they are listed because both
are part of how the binary is made. Nothing that only exists on another platform is listed at
all — a Windows build never compiles the macOS, Android, Wayland, or X11 crates that share the
lockfile.

**zet's own crates.** `zet-app`, `zet-config`, `zet-font`, `zet-input`, `zet-pty`, `zet-render`,
`zet-session`, `zet-ui`, and `zet-vt` are first-party code in this workspace and carry the root
licences. (`zet-update` is a workspace member as well, but nothing in `zet`'s dependency graph
uses it, so it is not in the binary at all.) There are no `[dev-dependencies]` in this
repository, and nothing from a test or benchmark target is compiled by a release build.

