## Fonts

The chrome — the titlebar, the tab strip, the menus — is drawn in IBM Plex Sans, and the two
weights it uses are compiled into the binary rather than loaded from the system. Both files are
the upstream release at version 3.005; zet registers their bytes into its own font stack
(`crates/zet-ui/src/fonts.rs`) and neither edits them nor runs a build step over them. Each file
states its own licence inside itself, in the `name` table a font carries, and points at
<http://scripts.sil.org/OFL>. `crates/zet-ui/assets/fonts/OFL.txt`, beside the fonts, is the
licence text reproduced at the end of this file.

**The reserved font name is "Plex."** IBM's notice reads "Copyright © 2017 IBM Corp. with
Reserved Font Name \"Plex\"", and the quoted word is the OFL's Reserved Font Name clause. That
clause restricts *modified* fonts: a modified version may not be presented to users under the
reserved name without written permission from IBM, and the restriction reaches only the primary
font name as shown to users. zet ships both files unmodified, does not subset or rename them, and
calls the family "IBM Plex Sans" everywhere it refers to the face, so the clause is not engaged.
The OFL conditions that do apply are met: each copy carries IBM's copyright notice and the
licence — here in this file, and in the fonts' own machine-readable `name` tables, which the OFL
accepts as a place to carry them — and the fonts are not being sold by themselves.

